# Lean
backends/leanregate/.lake/
backends/leanregate/build/
# lake-manifest.json is deliberately TRACKED: `leanprover/lean-action` refuses to
# configure without it ("No lake-manifest.json found"), which failed the leanregate
# job on every run. It also pins the exact Mathlib revision, so CI resolves the same
# dependencies the emitter was verified against instead of whatever is newest.
# runtime scratch: lean_prover/check_induction write proofs here. NOTE: the comment must be on
# its own line — .gitignore has no inline comments, so `Regate/  # ...` was one literal pattern
# and matched nothing, which is how these scratch files kept surfacing as untracked.
backends/leanregate/Regate/
# Build artifacts the Dockerfile generates (see leanregate/Dockerfile:37,47). `.lean_env` bakes
# ABSOLUTE LEAN_PATH/LD_LIBRARY_PATH for the machine that built it — committing it makes
# lean_prover take its direct-`lean` fast path with paths that do not exist anywhere else,
# which is exactly how CI ended up reporting `unknown module prefix 'Mathlib'`.
backends/leanregate/.lean_env

